<https://example.org/trendscout/source-record/2cc150d0-748d-599b-bf30-18f175d2773f> a ts:SourceRecord ;
    rdfs:subClassOf prov:Entity ;
    ts:about <https://example.org/trendscout/startup/langchain> ;
    ts:collectorVersion "mixed-corpus/1.0" ;
    ts:contentHash "b3cab4c63e72f17de3b312aba94dcd80dd0b937304531e1bd36f2eab3ca24238" ;
    ts:memberOfOrigin <https://example.org/trendscout/origin/dc1179c95d9a8130> ;
    ts:observedAt "2026-11-21T06:41:31+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    ts:originClusterId "dc1179c95d9a8130" ;
    ts:passage "ABOUT US At LangChain, our mission is to enable every company to own its intelligence. We believe agents will transform how companies operate, and we're building the foundation to make that future possible. Our open-source harnesses and LangSmith platform give developers and enterprises the infrastructure to run, improve, and govern agents at scale. We've raised $460M to date, with our most recent funding round valuing the company at $3B, backed by leading investors including Sequoia, Benchmark, IVP, and CapitalG. As we continue to expand our platform and tackle some of the hardest challenges in agent engineering, every team member has the opportunity to make a meaningful impact and help shape both our technology and the future of the industry. More than 7,000 organizations rely on LangSmith, from fast-growing startups to Fortune 500 enterprises, including NVIDIA, Bridgewater, LinkedIn, Workday, and Rippling. We're just getting started on making high-performing agents easier to build and manage at scale. ABOUT THE ROLE We're looking for a Product Designer to help shape the experience for the developers and teams who build on LangChain. You'll work across our core product surfaces, and depending on where the need is greatest, that could include how developers get from first signup to real production usage, as well as deeper platform workflows like debugging, evaluation, and observability. The common thread is developers doing technical, often high-stakes work, and needing an interface that gets out of their way. You'll partner with engineering, product, and other designers to figure out where the friction is and design your way out of it. *This position will be onsite in San Francisco, CA WHAT YOU'LL DO - Build a deep understanding of how developers actually use LangChain's products through interviews and feedback sessions so your design decisions are grounded in real behavior and address user needs - Own the full design arc on your features — from early concepts to polished, shipped work - Work across a range of product areas and design initiatives as priorities shift - Collaborate closely with product, engineering and other key stakeholders to ship new features quickly WHAT YOU'LL BRING - 3+ years of fullstack product design experience ideally working on developer tools, AI, or complex SaaS products - Sharp eye for detail, with a strong foundation across user-centered design, interaction design, and visual craft - A track record of solving hard interaction design problems, particularly around dense technical data - Data-driven decision making - you are comfortable driving user research, both with internal stakeholders and external customers, and using what you learn to inform your designs - You take initiative and ownership of tasks end-to-end - Strong technical acumen - you collaborate effectively with engineers to design things that are both well-crafted and feasible - Start-up DNA - you thrive in fast-paced, highly dynamic environments COMPENSATION PHILOSOPHY We offer competitive compensation that includes base salary, variable compensation for relevant roles, meaningful equity, benefits, and perks. We are hiring for this role across a range of scope, and the compensation band reflects that. Your offer depends on what we learn about your impact, craft, leadership, and communication during the interview process. We will tell you early where you’re tracking and talk comp with you before offer stage. Team members in the EU, UK, and APAC receive locally competitive benefits aligned with regional norms and regulations. BENEFITS Benefits include medical, dental, and vision coverage, flexible vacation, a 401(k) plan, meals on in-office days in the US and more." ;
