<https://example.org/trendscout/source-record/724f07a0-9038-5c04-a444-a224e9ba24d4> a ts:SourceRecord ;
    rdfs:subClassOf prov:Entity ;
    ts:about <https://example.org/trendscout/startup/langchain> ;
    ts:collectorVersion "mixed-corpus/1.0" ;
    ts:contentHash "37b975b010436b7587decee69d2c77f942fd0c565b89063d0ec56a67559b34b8" ;
    ts:memberOfOrigin <https://example.org/trendscout/origin/c45f26beb8528de4> ;
    ts:observedAt "2026-11-21T06:41:31+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    ts:originClusterId "c45f26beb8528de4" ;
    ts:passage "ABOUT US At LangChain, our mission is to enable every company to own its intelligence. We believe agents will transform how companies operate, and we're building the foundation to make that future possible. Our open-source harnesses and LangSmith platform give developers and enterprises the infrastructure to run, improve, and govern agents at scale. We've raised $460M to date, with our most recent funding round valuing the company at $3B, backed by leading investors including Sequoia, Benchmark, IVP, and CapitalG. As we continue to expand our platform and tackle some of the hardest challenges in agent engineering, every team member has the opportunity to make a meaningful impact and help shape both our technology and the future of the industry. More than 7,000 organizations rely on LangSmith, from fast-growing startups to Fortune 500 enterprises, including NVIDIA, Bridgewater, LinkedIn, Workday, and Rippling. We're just getting started on making high-performing agents easier to build and manage at scale. ABOUT THE ROLE Designs, builds and improves what the GTM Agent does to create pipeline, from the first signal about a prospect to a booked meeting. Owns the software and agents behind outbound on every channel: inbound lead follow-up, prospecting, multi-channel sequences, email deliverability, calling and the quality of every message the agent writes, with people deciding what goes out. Serves Sales Development Representatives (SDRs), Account Executives (AEs), their managers and Marketing. The goal of the role is business impact for those teams: more positive replies, more meetings booked and more qualified pipeline for every dollar spent. Additionally, this role has a communication and evangelizing component: showing the teams it serves what works, and sharing content and open source projects with our developer community. This role suits an engineer who has already built agents or software for outbound and prospecting, such as sequencing, email deliverability, dialing or AI-written outreach. WHAT YOU'LL DO - Spends time with SDRs, AEs and their managers to find the prospecting work they repeat that the agent can take over. - Designs, builds and improves the agent's outbound workflows: what starts each run, what the agent reads and decides, what it drafts, and what waits for a rep's approval. - Builds the agentic system that follows up every inbound lead within minutes: it qualifies the lead, researches the person and the account, and drafts a first touch for the owner the routing rules assign. - Builds and improves the system that runs Marketing's outbound plays and campaigns for every rep, from the target list to the first touch. - Builds the software and agentic system behind multi-channel sequences, which combine email, LinkedIn and calls, choose each next touch from what the prospect did, and stop when the prospect replies on any channel. - Builds the email sending and deliverability system: sending domains and mailboxes, warm-up, daily limits, address checks, bounces, opt-outs and inbox placement across mail providers. - Builds the calling software reps use: call lists, dialing and the research a rep reads before each call. - Owns the quality of what the agent writes, so every message fits the prospect's signal, their history with us and the right product, and uses how much reps edit each message and the replies it gets to find what to fix. - Builds the safeguards that keep prospects from getting duplicate or overlapping outreach, and the sync that logs every email, LinkedIn action and call in Salesforce. - Builds experiments that test messages, channels, timing and sequences against held-out groups, measures which ones book meetings, and fixes or removes what doesn't. - Writes evals for every feature shipped, and ships each feature with its scorecard row. - Shows reps and their managers what works, and shares it through blog posts, webinars and open source. WHAT YOU'LL BRING - AI-Native Developer: You have a deep understanding of the LLM stack: prompting, retrieval (RAG), cognitive architectures, and agentic loops. You have likely already built with LangChain or LangGraph. - Engineering Foundation: You are a strong software engineer (typically 3+ years) with at least 1 year of experience specifically shipping LLM systems in production. - Self-Directed \"Founder\" Mentality: You don't need a ticket to tell you what to fix. You are comfortable navigating ambiguity, identifying high-impact problems, and driving them to completion autonomously. - Full-Stack Capability: Strong coding skills in Python or TypeScript (ideally both) and the ability to build end-to-end applications. - Customer-Centric: You enjoy the intersection of high-level engineering and direct customer impact. You can translate a customer's technical pain point into a scalable system architecture. NICE TO HAVES - Expertise with LangSmith for evaluation and monitoring. - Experience building or maintaining open-source projects. - A background in technical consulting, solutions engineering, or high-growth GTM teams. COMPENSATION PHILOSOPHY We offer competitive compensation that includes base salary, variable compensation for relevant roles, meaningful equity, benefits, and perks. We are hiring for this role across a range of scope, and the compensation band reflects that. Your offer depends on what we learn about your impact, craft, leadership, and communication during the interview process. We will tell you early where you’re tracking and talk comp with you before offer stage. Team members in the EU, UK, and APAC receive locally competitive benefits aligned with regional norms and regulations. BENEFITS Benefits include medical, dental, and vision coverage, flexible vacation, a 401(k) plan, meals on in-office days in the US and more." ;
    ts:publishedAt "2026-11-20T16:03:56+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    ts:publishedBy <https://example.org/trendscout/publisher/langchain> ;
    ts:recordId "724f07a0-9038-5c04-a444-a224e9ba24d4" ;
    ts:sourceType "job" ;
    ts:sourceUrl "https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/langchain/32c6fe13-76e0-49a2-849d-991014416987"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    ts:title "Agent Engineer, Pre-sales" .

<https://example.org/trendscout/source-record/7db42262-253c-50c2-b41a-40aa32637d12> a ts:SourceRecord ;
    rdfs:subClassOf prov:Entity ;
    ts:about <https://example.org/trendscout/startup/llamaindex> ;
    ts:collectorVersion "mixed-corpus/1.0" ;
    ts:contentHash "6c6a65e0107ae313ff3733930a6a31a6e898fb3a448bec18f64afa62fa6deb77" ;
    ts:memberOfOrigin <https://example.org/trendscout/origin/81e282364a0aecda> ;
    ts:observedAt "2026-11-21T06:41:31+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    ts:originClusterId "81e282364a0aecda" ;
    ts:passage "Join us and help shape the future of AI by defining the narrative around document understanding. ABOUT THE ROLE We are looking for an AI Research Engineer to join our document understanding team. This role is ideal for someone who sits between applied research and strong engineering. You will work on vision-language models, document processing, data curation, synthetic data generation, benchmarking, training, fine-tuning, and post-training. The goal is simple: make our document AI systems more accurate, faster, and more cost-effective in production. You should be excited by frontier AI work, but equally motivated by practical product impact. This is not a pure research role where ideas stay in papers. You will be expected to prototype quickly, evaluate rigorously, and help turn promising approaches into production systems used by customers. WHAT YOU’LL DO - Develop and train vision-language models for document processing and document understanding. - Build data pipelines for data curation, synthetic data generation, labeling, and benchmark creation. - Evaluate base models and perform post-training or fine-tuning to hit specific performance targets. - Improve model accuracy, latency, and cost-effectiveness across real-world document workflows. - Design and maintain benchmarks to measure extraction quality, layout understanding, OCR performance, reasoning accuracy, and end-to-end system reliability. - Work with messy real-world documents, including PDFs, scanned documents, tables, charts, forms, and multi-page enterprise documents. - Collaborate with engineering to move successful research prototypes into production. - Work directly with customers when needed to translate product requirements into benchmarks, experiments, and model improvements. - Stay close to the latest research in vision-language models, document AI, post-training, synthetic data, and agentic systems. - Use modern AI coding workflows and tools to move quickly. WHAT WE’RE LOOKING FOR - 3–7 years of experience in machine learning engineering, applied research, or research engineering. - Strong ML foundation, including hands-on experience benchmarking and training models. - Strong Python skills and comfort with modern ML tooling, especially PyTorch. - Experience with computer vision, vision-language models, NLP, document AI, OCR, extraction, or agentic AI systems. - Ability to build experiments, evaluate results, and iterate quickly toward measurable performance improvements. - Strong engineering judgment and ability to write clean, production-quality code. - Comfort working in a fast-paced startup environment with high ownership and limited structure. - Adaptable, scrappy, and self-directed — someone who can figure things out without waiting to be told. - Strong technical writing and communication skills. NICE TO HAVE - Prior startup experience, especially at an early-stage or high-growth AI company. - Experience as a founder or early startup engineer. - Experience building or improving document processing systems. - Experience with synthetic data generation, post-training, fine-tuning, or benchmark design. - Familiarity with tools such as vLLM, Pydantic, uv, ruff, mypy, Claude Code, Cursor, or similar modern AI engineering workflows. - Experience with open-source AI infrastructure or developer tools. WHO YOU’LL WORK WITH You will work closely with the CTO and the document understanding team, partnering across research, engineering, product, and customer-facing teams. WHY JOIN LLAMAINDEX - Work on a core AI infrastructure problem: making complex documents understandable and actionable for AI systems. - Build production systems at the frontier of vision-language models and document AI. - Join a fast-growing startup with strong open-source adoption and commercial traction. - Work directly with technical founders and a highly ambitious engineering team. - Have real ownership over model quality, product capability, and technical direction. Pursuant to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records. LlamaIndex does not accept unsolicited agency resumes. Please do not forward resumes to our jobs alias, employees, or any other organization location. LlamaIndex is not responsible for any fees related to unsolicited resumes." ;
    ts:publishedAt "2026-07-08T01:11:47+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    ts:publishedBy <https://example.org/trendscout/publisher/llamaindex> ;
    ts:recordId "7db42262-253c-50c2-b41a-40aa32637d12" ;
    ts:sourceType "job" ;
    ts:sourceUrl "https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/llamaindex/5ef32675-090d-4eb2-bca0-ddb6fbde0215"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    ts:title "Member of Technical Staff, Applied Research" .

<https://example.org/trendscout/source-record/8040d79a-d5bc-57b8-80ed-3b703a3d7af3> a ts:SourceRecord ;
    rdfs:subClassOf prov:Entity ;
    ts:about <https://example.org/trendscout/startup/llamaindex> ;
    ts:collectorVersion "mixed-corpus/1.0" ;
    ts:contentHash "0efe3585815f7221a7d9c2e33e644fefd10fa64828238aa323e9989d57c52429" ;
    ts:memberOfOrigin <https://example.org/trendscout/origin/c2a54454ce909698> ;
    ts:observedAt "2026-11-21T06:41:31+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    ts:originClusterId "c2a54454ce909698" ;
    ts:passage "Follow us on 4 Today we’re delighted to announce two milestones: the general availability of LlamaParse, and our $19M series A funding round. LlamaParse is the core of our enterprise offering: a turn-key solution for agentic knowledge management over your unstructured data. It’s the most secure, accurate, and easy to use platform to enable building knowledge agents. Use one of our hundreds of available integrations to connect to your enterprise data, and let us take care of parsing, ingesting, indexing, and retrieval for you, as well as uptime and reliability. LlamaParse is available both as an instant-setup SaaS offering and an on-premise solution for higher security and data locality guarantees. It’s also highly private and secure, with SOC 2 Type 2 certification. Now in general availability, you can sign up today and join happy customers like Rakuten, Carlyle, Salesforce and KPMG. If you’re in the EU, you may be interested in our GDPR-compliant EU SaaS offering , featuring guaranteed EU data residency. Ready to get started with LlamaParse? Explore our free and paid plans today. Learn more LlamaParse is powered by LlamaParse, our industry-leading solution for parsing complex, unstructured document formats like PDFs, Word documents, PowerPoints, and hundreds of other formats. LlamaParse takes care of complex elements like tables, charts and images with ease, and has handled hundreds of millions of documents for tens of thousands of satisfied users already. Learn more about LlamaParse . You can build on top of LlamaParse and LlamaParse using the LlamaIndex framework, our leading open-source framework in Python and TypeScript . We’ve got more than 3 million monthly downloads, almost 40,000 GitHub stars, and hundreds of thousands of active developers worldwide. Our event-driven Workflows architecture makes it easy to put together scalable, predictable AI agents, and developers love it! Our series A is led by Norwest Venture Partners, with participation from our existing investors Greylock Partners, bringing our total capital raised to $27.5M. Dave Zilberman, general partner at Norwest Venture Partners, says “LlamaIndex is compelling for Norwest as we’ve been closely studying enterprise requirements for AI adoption, specifically around data preparation, ingestion and custom agents as part of an ongoing investment thesis. The founding team has demonstrated grit and resilience, building usable, enterprise-enabling capabilities to solve critical pain points—from production accuracy issues to scaling complex data workflows. With customers already lined up, LlamaIndex has the potential to empower the agentic enterprise. We’re excited to see where the next year takes them.\" With our new injection of funding, we’re going to be expanding our team! We’re hiring in all sorts of positions to expand our OSS frameworks, further improve LlamaParse, go even deeper on LlamaParse, and accelerate our go-to-market. Check out our open positions !" ;
    ts:publishedBy <https://example.org/trendscout/publisher/llamaindex> ;
    ts:recordId "8040d79a-d5bc-57b8-80ed-3b703a3d7af3" ;
    ts:sourceType "funding" ;
    ts:sourceUrl "https://llamaindex.ai/blog/announcing-our-series-a-and-llamacloud-general-availability"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    ts:title "Series A Funding And LlamaParse GA Update | LlamaIndex" .

