<https://example.org/trendscout/source-record/eb174b5a-a28e-5260-a99a-aeb84f1e4be8> a ts:SourceRecord ;
    rdfs:subClassOf prov:Entity ;
    ts:about <https://example.org/trendscout/startup/langchain> ;
    ts:collectorVersion "mixed-corpus/1.0" ;
    ts:contentHash "96ed00b400b000ec443765282f1d8f6afe41e6dd112206d2b7f697a56422cead" ;
    ts:memberOfOrigin <https://example.org/trendscout/origin/97db7b651f0fccb8> ;
    ts:observedAt "2026-11-21T06:41:31+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    ts:originClusterId "97db7b651f0fccb8" ;
    ts:passage "LangChain Raises $300M Series C at $3B Valuation Would you notice if your agent got worse in production? Tell us in our annual survey for the chance to win LangChain swag. | Take survey ↗ Products LangSmith Platform Agent Improvement Engine Improve agents autonomously Observability See exactly what your agents are doing Evaluation Score and improve agent performance Agent Runtime Agent Server Ship and scale agents in production Sandboxes Run agent-generated code safely Fleet Agents for the whole company Agent Governance LLM Gateway Control agent model calls Open Source Agent Frameworks deepagents Build long-running agents for complex tasks langgraph Build agents with low-level control langchain Quick start agents with any model provider Resources Learn Academy Free courses on building agents Certification Become a certified agent engineer Blog Product news and deep dives Documentation Guides and API references Library Guides, reports, and ebooks Max Agency Podcast on building agents Webinars Live and recorded expert sessions YouTube Video tutorials and walkthroughs Interrupt On-Demand Recorded sessions from Interrupt events Connect Community Connect with other agent builders Meetups Local, community-led gatherings Events Find events online and near you LangChain @ AWS re:Invent Nov 30 · Las Vegas Docs Customers Pricing Try LangSmith Get a demo Try LangSmith Get a demo Company Announcements LangChain Raises $300M to Enable Every Company to Own Its Intelligence Harrison Chase November 13, 2026 3 min Go back to blog Create agents Create agents Share Our Series C Announcement Today, we’re announcing that LangChain raised $300M at a $3B valuation to advance our mission to enable every company to own its intelligence. The round was led by existing investor CapitalG, with significant participation from new investors GIC and DFJ Growth and existing investors IVP and Sapphire Ventures. We believe agents will transform the economy. That future will be shaped by domain-specific agents differentiated by their knowledge, data, and UX. These agents will be sold as standalone products and also used to transform internal company operations. The companies that control these systems will build lasting competitive advantages. To capture that opportunity, every company will need to own its intelligence. Companies should be free to choose the best models for their needs, control their data and infrastructure, and continuously improve their agents, while maintaining the governance needed to operate securely at scale. That’s why we’ve built LangSmith, the framework-agnostic platform to run, improve, and govern agents . More than 7,000 organizations already rely on LangSmith, from fast-growing startups like Harvey, Rippling, and Listen Labs to Fortune 500 enterprises like NVIDIA, Toyota, and Salesforce. Clay uses LangSmith to monitor hundreds of millions of agent runs per month and improve their agents. Workday uses LangSmith to run and govern agents across the organization, reducing the time to deploy a new agent from five months to under a day. LangSmith provides the foundation for companies to control their agent systems across three pillars – Agent Runtime, Agent Improvement, and Agent Governance: Agent Runtime gives teams the architecture and infrastructure to run agents reliably. Deep Agents, LangGraph, and LangChain give developers flexibility across models and control over how context is managed. LangSmith Agent Server and Sandboxes allow teams to deploy and run agents securely at scale, whether in the cloud or in their environment. LangSmith Managed Agents and Fleet provide fully managed services to build, deploy, and run mission-critical agents in production. Agent Improvement helps teams test, monitor, and improve agent performance. LangSmith Observability and Evaluation give teams visibility into how agents behave and measure quality. LangSmith Engine, our in-platform agent, automates improvement by finding errors, writing code and prompt fixes, and monitoring production traffic for regressions. LangSmith Fine-Tuning helps teams turn agent traces into training data to fine-tune and evaluate specialized models. Agent Governance gives teams centralized control over how agents use models, tools, and data. Our LLM and Tool Gateways help teams manage model budgets and fallbacks, protect sensitive data, and govern tool access and authentication across teams and agents . On Friday, November 20th, we shared several new LangSmith capabilities that build on this foundation. Watch the recording of our special release event to see what’s coming next. LangSmith has been shaped by our fantastic community – from our developer evangelists to the customers we’re lucky enough to partner with. Thank you all for your feedback, insights, and trust. There’s still so much left to build. Building high performing agents is harder than it should be, and we‘re determined to change that. Come join us in making it easier for every company to own its intelligence. Harrison ‍ Thank you to our new and existing investors for helping make this journey possible. We’re excited to welcome Salesforce Ventures, Insight Venture Partners, QuantumLight, and MongoDB Ventures, and grateful to Sequoia, Amplify, and Benchmark for doubling down in this round. ‍ Related content Company Announcements Observability & Evals LangSmith for Coding Agents: Now track spend by outcome Jacob Lee November 18, 2026 8 min Company Announcements Protect sensitive data in your traces: new controls in LangSmith Trammell Saltzgaber November 17, 2026 5 min LangSmith Company Announcements New in LangSmith: Engine v2, Managed Deep Agents, Fine-Tuning, and More Jacob Talbot September 25, 2026 7 min Sign up for our newsletter to stay up to date Thank you! Your submission has been received! Oops! Something went wrong while submitting the form. See what your agent is really doing LangSmith, our agent engineering platform, helps developers debug every agent decision, eval changes, and deploy in one click. Try LangSmith Get a demo Products LangSmith Platform LangSmith Observability LangSmith Evaluation LangSmith Agent Server LangSmith Fleet LangSmith Sandboxes Deep Agents Deep Agents Code LangChain LangGraph Resources Blog Customer Stories Guides Community Changelog Docs Support LangChain Academy Company About Careers Partners Trust Center Brand Assets Events Sign up for our newsletter to stay up to date Thank you! Your submission has been received! Oops! Something went wrong while submitting the form. All systems operational Privacy policy Enterprise Terms Enterprise DPA Standard Terms Standard DPA" ;
    ts:publishedAt "2026-11-13T15:55:00+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    ts:publishedBy <https://example.org/trendscout/publisher/langchain> ;
    ts:recordId "eb174b5a-a28e-5260-a99a-aeb84f1e4be8" ;
    ts:sourceType "funding" ;
    ts:sourceUrl "https://langchain.com/blog/series-c"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    ts:title "LangChain Raises $300M Series C at $3B Valuation" .

<https://example.org/trendscout/source-record/ee48465f-09e2-5c88-8bff-dc68032962cd> a ts:SourceRecord ;
    rdfs:subClassOf prov:Entity ;
    ts:about <https://example.org/trendscout/startup/langchain> ;
    ts:collectorVersion "mixed-corpus/1.0" ;
    ts:contentHash "c6e926da31d09556f6993f19e0caeaa9f2c70087ae268739735e902cfdc74cfc" ;
    ts:memberOfOrigin <https://example.org/trendscout/origin/025561ed685c47fd> ;
    ts:observedAt "2026-11-21T06:41:31+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    ts:originClusterId "025561ed685c47fd" ;
    ts:passage "ABOUT US At LangChain, our mission is to enable every company to own its intelligence. We believe agents will transform how companies operate, and we're building the foundation to make that future possible. Our open-source harnesses and LangSmith platform give developers and enterprises the infrastructure to run, improve, and govern agents at scale. We've raised $460M to date, with our most recent funding round valuing the company at $3B, backed by leading investors including Sequoia, Benchmark, IVP, and CapitalG. As we continue to expand our platform and tackle some of the hardest challenges in agent engineering, every team member has the opportunity to make a meaningful impact and help shape both our technology and the future of the industry. More than 7,000 organizations rely on LangSmith, from fast-growing startups to Fortune 500 enterprises, including NVIDIA, Bridgewater, LinkedIn, Workday, and Rippling. We're just getting started on making high-performing agents easier to build and manage at scale. ABOUT THE ROLE The LangSmith team owns and builds LangChain's core platform for observability, evaluation, and production reliability of AI systems. From tracing and annotation to run rules, evaluations, and beyond, this team owns LangSmith end-to-end. If you want to define what great AI observability looks like at production scale, this is where that work gets done. We're looking for a Product Manager to own key parts of LangSmith. Building AI products is changing the way software teams work; LangSmith is the observability, evals and deployment platform that makes shipping reliable AI systems possible. WHAT YOU'LL DO This role sits at the intersection of user experience and production infrastructure. You'll partner with engineers to build features that feel intuitive while solving deeply technical problems: versioning complex prompt chains, debugging multi-step agent failures, or designing evaluation systems that scale from 10 to 10,000 test cases. You'll work directly with customers — from early-stage startups shipping their first agent to enterprises running mission-critical AI systems — to understand where the platform breaks down and what capabilities unlock new workflows. - Own the roadmap for a core area of the LangSmith platform. - Work with customers to understand their challenges and define new product features. - Work with engineering to define scope, make technical tradeoffs, and ship high-impact features quickly. - Help shape product strategy alongside our founders and leadership team. WHAT YOU'LL BRING - 3+ years of product management or engineering experience, ideally building developer tools, infrastructure products, or technical SaaS platforms. - Deeply technical — you can hold your own in conversations about API design, system architecture, data pipelines, and debugging production issues. - Bias toward action — you'd rather ship, learn, and iterate than build the perfect solution upfront. - Strong written and verbal communicator who can align cross-functional teams around a shared vision. NICE TO HAVE - Computer Science, Engineering, or equivalent technical background. - Previous experience at a high-growth startup or developer-focused company. - Hands-on experience building with LLMs, agents, or AI applications. COMPENSATION PHILOSOPHY We offer competitive compensation that includes base salary, variable compensation for relevant roles, meaningful equity, benefits, and perks. We are hiring for this role across a range of scope, and the compensation band reflects that. Your offer depends on what we learn about your impact, craft, leadership, and communication during the interview process. We will tell you early where you’re tracking and talk comp with you before offer stage. Team members in the EU, UK, and APAC receive locally competitive benefits aligned with regional norms and regulations. BENEFITS Benefits include medical, dental, and vision coverage, flexible vacation, a 401(k) plan, meals on in-office days in the US and more." ;
    ts:publishedAt "2026-10-21T12:40:00+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    ts:publishedBy <https://example.org/trendscout/publisher/langchain> ;
    ts:recordId "ee48465f-09e2-5c88-8bff-dc68032962cd" ;
    ts:sourceType "job" ;
    ts:sourceUrl "https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/langchain/27af5f96-b287-4bcc-8679-f96686dc7c8d"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    ts:title "Product Manager, LangSmith" .

<https://example.org/trendscout/source-record/f3b13310-8958-5220-8e75-21518ee410bb> a ts:SourceRecord ;
